# Magic Mouse 2 (Apple 004C:0269) over Bluetooth. The gesture daemon
# (magic-mouse-gestures) reads the raw HID node, which carries every touch and
# button press, so grant the active seat user an ACL instead of upstream's
# MODE="0666" -- that exposed the stream to any local process.
#
# MODE="0600" is stated explicitly rather than left to the default: udev only
# applies a mode when a rule asks for one, so dropping upstream's 0666 rule did
# not by itself take world access back off an already-created node.
#
# Must be numbered below 73: /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/73-seat-late.rules is what
# turns the uaccess tag into an ACL (RUN{builtin}+="uaccess"), so a 99- file
# would add the tag after that rule has already run.
KERNEL=="hidraw*", KERNELS=="0005:004C:0269.*", MODE="0600", TAG+="uaccess"
